WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.888
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.888 --> 00:00:05.275
which takes about sixty
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:07.650
You'll state the program's ownership rule,

4
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.025
and which owners the code counts as valid.

5
00:00:10.025 --> 00:00:12.514
You'll explain D N P 2, the orphan rule,

6
00:00:12.514 --> 00:00:17.150
and how it differs from the program's
own policy for orphaned apps.

7
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.288
You'll run the ownership check and
read its findings and its orphan plan.

8
00:00:21.288 --> 00:00:25.628
And you'll show that the write path
only dry-runs without the Apply switch,

9
00:00:25.628 --> 00:00:28.376
and refuses a plan whose
hash nobody approved.

10
00:00:28.376 --> 00:00:34.000
Before you start, finish Module 1, because
this module checks Module 1's register.

11
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.294
And read the guide's record
each identity joins to,

12
00:00:37.294 --> 00:00:39.463
for the owner and sponsor fields.

13
00:00:39.463 --> 00:00:45.562
Lab 1 needs PowerShell 7.1 or later with
Pester 5, and a clone of the repository.

14
00:00:45.562 --> 00:00:46.540
No tenant.
